  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Jitendra Kumar vs State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief Secy. ... on 21 March, 2024 Author: Manish Kumar Bench: Manish Kumar High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:24979 Court No. - 18 Case :- Writ - A No. - 2372 of 2024 Petitioner :- Jitendra Kumar Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief Secy. Food Safety Drug Admin. U.P. Lko And Counsel for Petitioner :- Avinash Tiwari Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C. Hon'ble Manish Kumar,J. 1.",
    "facts": "3. Present petition has been preferred for issuing a direction to the respondents not to treat Special Adverse Entry dated 08.08.2022 as adverse report against the petitioner for the purposes of granting service benefits as per Rule 5 of the U.P. Government Servants (Disposal of Representation against Adverse Annual Confidential Reports and Allied Matters) Rules, 1995 (hereinafter referred to as, the Rules, 1995). 4.",
    "arguments": "Learned Counsel for the petitioner has submitted that the petitioner was initially appointed on Jitendra Kumar vs State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief Secy. ... on 21 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/160699741/ 1 the post of Food Inspector (now designated as Food Safety Officer) in the year 1998 and confirmed on the post subsequently. 6. It is further submitted that in December, 2023 petitioner has competed 26 years of service thus he is entitled and eligible for grant of 3rd A.C.P. and other service benefits in pursuance of the Government Order dated 05.11.2014 but due to Special Adverse Entry, the petitioner may not get the same. 7. On the other hand learned Standing Counsel has submitted that till the Special Adverse Entry passed against the petitioner will not be [LEAKAGE_MASK], he is not entitled for any service benefits."
  },
